  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: double free in sftp_open() lets a malicious SSH server\n     corrupt the heap of an authenticated client opening an SFTP session\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-66032.patch: set data to NULL after freeing the\n       SSH_FXP_STATUS response buffer on the FX_OK path, so the if(badness)\n       arm cannot free the same pointer a second time when the follow-up\n       sftp_packet_require() for SSH_FXP_HANDLE fails, in sftp_open() in\n       src/sftp.c\n     - CVE-2026-66032",
